    <string name="setup_help_app_health_quick">Checks encrypted preferences, looks for a crash log, and confirms an API key is available (embedded build key or Settings).</string>
    <string name="setup_help_app_health_fix">Clear app cache only if support asks. If last_crash.txt exists, note the first line and reinstall the latest APK. Add sk-ant key in Settings if missing.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_shop_desk_quick">Pings your Shop Desk ingest URL (default http://PC-IP:8791). The office PC must run the Shop Desk receiver on the same Wi‑Fi.</string>
    <string name="setup_help_shop_desk_fix">Verify PC IP in Settings → Shop Desk URL. On PC run the receiver script. Allow Windows Firewall inbound on port 8791. Retry GET /api/health in Chrome on the tablet.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_link_transport_quick">Lists USB OBD adapters and runs a non-destructive detectUsbKind probe. No vehicle communication required for a pass when no cable is attached.</string>
    <string name="setup_help_link_transport_fix">Grant USB permission when prompted. Reseat DB15 cable. If Launch/X431 hangs, force-stop the OEM app (Settings → Apps). Try Settings → Native OBD → Use VCI transport on Launch tablets.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_camera_quick">Opens the same camera capture flow used in New Session. Saves one test JPEG to verify FileProvider and permission.</string>
    <string name="setup_help_camera_fix">Allow camera permission. Tap capture manually — do not background the app mid-shot. Use shop lights; wipe lens. Skip with reason if hardware is unavailable.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_session_bootstrap_quick">Runs a silent session link probe (Plan A Launch bridge vs direct path) without starting a customer session.</string>
    <string name="setup_help_session_bootstrap_fix">Enable accessibility for Together Car Works. Open Launch once and dismiss splash. Check Settings → Use Launch for vehicle link (Plan A). Re-run after USB probe passes.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_harvest_path_quick">Dry-run: confirms vehicle DB paths are readable and a harvest manifest can be built (no ZIP upload).</string>
    <string name="setup_help_harvest_path_fix">Grant All files access. Open the OEM diagnostic app and connect to a vehicle once so DB folders exist. Then use Settings → Transfer data → Zip files.</string>

    <string name="setup_help_tier4_trial_quick">Tier 4 trial enables programming reference checklists for Ford, Jeep, Dodge, Ram, and Chrysler only — not automated flash.</string>
    <string name="setup_help_tier4_trial_fix">Read the trial notice and tap Accept. For GM/Toyota/Honda marques, Tier 4 stays disabled until a full license — use Plan B reference screens instead.</string>

